From 4341618f54c0bdf6f632d730431509302304c765 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Fink <chris@cxjxf.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 07:44:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: size the Windows exception stack reserve from the
 host

Windows dispatches an exception on the faulting goroutine's stack: the
kernel pushes an EXCEPTION_RECORD and a CONTEXT below SP, and ntdll and
sigtramp run there until sigtrampgo switches to g0. stackSystem reserves
4 KiB for this. But the CONTEXT holds the extended CPU state the OS
enabled, about 1.7 KiB on most CPUs, 3.4 KiB with AVX-512 and 11.7 KiB
with AMX. On AMX hosts the frame overruns the stack and corrupts the
heap.

Make stackSystem, stackGuard and fixedStack variables. On Windows,
osinit sets stackSystem to the CONTEXT size InitializeContext reports
plus 2 KiB for the rest of the dispatch, and never below the old 4 KiB.
Assembly that sets up g0 uses the compile-time stackGuardStatic until
mstart0 or minit sets the guard.

shrinkstack also refuses to leave less than stackSystem below SP.

Fixes #81238

Change-Id: I46051a7d94205f85193615c2e37a29d5c025f67a
